! X resources — loaded by dwm-session.sh with `xrdb -merge` before any client
! starts (dwm opens its fonts once, at startup, so order matters).
!
! 96dpi is the standard Xft/GTK baseline. 110 was tried to compensate for the
! eDP-1 panel (309mm x 173mm at 1920x1080 = 157dpi), but this session also
! drives a 27-inch 1920x1080 HDMI panel at ~82dpi: at 110 everything there —
! GTK chrome, Firefox tabs, the wezterm tab bar — rendered visibly oversized.
! 96 keeps the UI at the familiar 1:1 size. Raise in small steps (100, 104)
! if the laptop panel alone feels too small; keep gtk_theme.sh in sync.
Xft.dpi: 96

! Rendering: subpixel RGB + light hinting is the sharpest text this panel
! produces; sharper glyph edges read as brighter at the same nits. GTK3 does
! not read these (it asks fontconfig directly), so configs/fontconfig/fonts.conf
! declares the same choices for it.
Xft.antialias: true
Xft.hinting: true
Xft.hintstyle: hintslight
Xft.rgba: rgb
Xft.lcdfilter: lcddefault
